Title: Module 10 - Multiplot Visualisation: Regional Logistics & Fulfillment Dynamics
Date: October 27, 2026
Summary of the Exercise: In this exercise, I explored intentional multiplot design by combining two related data visualisations into a publication-ready interactive display.
The workflow was completed in the following stages:
Directory Setup: Established a dedicated workspace folder (Module 10 - Portfolio Exercise) within my OneDrive portfolio structure, maintaining clean separation for scripts, datasets, data cards, and write-ups.
Data Sourcing & Processing: Structured spatial and statistical performance metrics across key suburban hubs in South-East Melbourne. Using Python (pandas), I processed suburban coordinates, order volumes, and average delivery durations to construct a cohesive regional dataset.
Interactive Visualisation Design: Developed a Python-based multiplot display using Plotly make_subplots. I paired a spatial coordinate map (Longitude vs. Latitude with scaled order volume markers) alongside a synchronized statistical bar chart tracking average delivery times, incorporating hover tooltips and interactive panning/zooming.
Hosting & Embedding: Exported the display as a standalone interactive .html file, deployed it via Posit Connect Cloud, and embedded the live application directly into this portfolio page.

